# Spike Test - BONANZA's SPIKES test course (SPEC.md 137.38), built only by the BZSPIKE=1 knob, as
# water.bbc is by BZWATER=1.  NOT a shipped course: the knob adds it to BZ_COURSES and makes it the
# pathway's pad 0, so a new game rests on it (title, Play Game, Enter).  Not on the TOUR.
#
# START is a plate at 2 units with a pad for each ball and the finish (exit 0) beside the start.  From it:
#  - east, the SPIKE CORRIDOR (wy 5 - 7): six cells of spikes the whole width, on to a goal (exit 1).
#    Steel is pushed up onto the tips and rolls on; rubber POPS and glass SHATTERS (and respawns) - too long
#    to Hop;
#  - south, the POPSPIKE LANE (wx 5 - 7): two rows of pop-up spikes, 64 steps up in every 128, the rows
#    half a period and three steps apart, each row's three cells a step apart (one pose change a step): cross a row
#    while it is down (a dead end: the finish clock rule keeps the goals by the one clock);
#  - south-east, the MEMBRANE BRIDGE (wy 9): four cells of crystal film over the void to a plate
#    (a dead end): glass rolls across it, rubber and steel fall through;
#  - north-east, the WATER PAIRING (the owner's: two steel-only mechanisms): a walkway 2 units up, past the spike corridor, whose one
#    water cell sinks steel down its column and out of the arch onto spikes - steel rides them to the yard.
course SPIKE "Spike Test"
music fairway    # a test course: SPEC.md 137.50.3, every course names its song
width  128
origin 320
ball   rubber

uses spike water

floor rect 4 4 10 10 flat 2   # the start plate
floor rect 10 5 19 8 flat 2   # the spike corridor
floor rect 5 10 8 19 flat 2   # the popspike lane
floor rect 10 9 14 10 flat 2   # the membrane bridge
floor rect 14 9 17 12 flat 2   # ...its far plate
floor rect 19 5 20 7 flat 2   # the corridor's end on to the walkway
floor rect 20 4 25 7 flat 2   # the water walkway, 2 units up
floor rect 20 7 25 14 flat 0   # the yard below it

prop spikes 11 5 17 8
prop popspikes 5 12 period 128 on 64 seed 0
prop popspikes 6 12 period 128 on 64 seed 1
prop popspikes 7 12 period 128 on 64 seed 2
prop popspikes 5 15 period 128 on 64 seed 67
prop popspikes 6 15 period 128 on 64 seed 68
prop popspikes 7 15 period 128 on 64 seed 69
prop membrane 10 9 14 10

water tile 22 6 top 2 bed 0
arch 22 6 +y
prop spikes 21 8 24 10

pad rubber 5 5
pad steel 7 5
pad glass 5 7
start 6 7
goal tile 8 8 flat 2
goal tile 18 6 flat 2 exit 1
clock 9 4
clock 17 7
limit 99
target 60
way 6 7
way 8 8
